20.This is optimal because to verify bipartiteness, every edge must be checked—a single edge forming an odd cycle can invalidate the graph.
21.If two adjacent nodes have the same color, a conflict is found (odd cycle exists), so return false immediately. Otherwise, continue traversal.
22.Disconnected graph ho sakta hai, isliye har unvisited node se BFS/DFS start karo—agar kisi bhi component me conflict mile to graph bipartite nahi hai.
23.Har unvisited node se BFS start karke 2-coloring karo; agar kisi edge par same-color neighbors mil jaayein to false, warna sab components pass ho jaayein to graph bipartite (true).
24.Har connected component par BFS se 2-coloring karo; agar kisi edge ke dono ends same color ho jaayein to bipartite nahi, warna bipartite.
25.Graph ko bipartite check karne ke liye har connected component par BFS + 2-coloring lagao; agar kisi edge ke dono endpoints same color ho jaayen, to answer false, warna true.
